{title: Oh! Susanna}
{artist: Stephen Foster, 1848}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, americana}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [G]come from Alabama with my [D]banjo on my [G]knee
I'm going to Louisiana, my [D]true love for to [G]see
It rained all night the day I left, the [D]weather it was [G]dry
The sun so hot I froze to death, Su[D]sanna, don't you [G]cry

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Oh! Su[G]sanna, oh [D]don't you cry for me
For [G]I come from Alabama with my [D]banjo on my [G]knee

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [G]had a dream the other night, when [D]everything was [G]still
I thought I saw Susanna, a-[D]coming down the [G]hill
The buckwheat cake was in her mouth, the [D]tear was in her [G]eye
Says I, I'm coming from the south, Su[D]sanna, don't you [G]cry

{chorus}
